# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .claspignore -- controls exactly what `clasp push` uploads to Apps Script.
#
# MECHANISM (verified against the installed clasp 3.4.1, which evaluates these
# patterns with micromatch.not(files, patterns, {dot:true})):
#
#   **/**        -> ignore EVERYTHING (all files, all subdirectories, dotfiles)
#   !<pattern>   -> re-include only that pattern
#
# A single `*` does NOT cross a path separator, so `!*.js` matches ONLY
# root-level .js files. That is the guarantee: the Apps Script backend lives in
# the repository root, and therefore NOTHING inside any subdirectory
# (frontend/, tests/, docs/, node_modules/) can ever be pushed.
#
# To verify: run `clasp status` (lists what would be pushed) or
# `node tests/claspignore.test.js`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Start by ignoring everything
**/**

# --- Re-include only the Apps Script backend (repository root) ---
!appsscript.json
!*.js
!*.gs

# --- Defensive exclusions, explicit for auditability ---
# Local dependency trees (clasp's own default only covers the root one)
node_modules/**
**/node_modules/**

# The future React + TypeScript + Vite frontend
frontend/**
**/frontend/**

# Non-backend directories
tests/**
docs/**
.git/**

# Files that document or configure the repo, never Apps Script
*.md
.clasp.json
.claspignore
.gitignore
package.json
package-lock.json